Since its founding, Neros Technologies has strategically raised $45.9 million across 2 funding rounds, leveraging partnerships with leading venture capital firms and prominent investors. The company's funding history includes an initial seed round to jumpstart product development and a significant Series A round that fueled further innovation and manufacturing expansion. Neros Technologies funding milestones include rapid scaling of their R&D and manufacturing facilities, as well as securing pivotal defense sector partnerships. Across each round, Neros Technologies pursued a focused funding strategy to support its vision of unmanned superiority at scale.

## Funding Rounds

### Series A - $35M - 2025-03-18 [...] ## Funding Rounds

### Series A - $35M - 2025-03-18

The Series A round was led by Vy Capital and raised $35 million to accelerate product development and support the expansion of manufacturing and international market presence. Funds were primarily allocated toward scaling production capabilities, enhancing battlefield drone technology resilience, and entering new defense sectors.

### Seed - $10.9M - 2024-05-20

Led by Sequoia Capital, this $10.9 million seed round provided the initial capital for Neros Technologies' product launch and early development efforts. The funding helped the company establish its core team, set up headquarters in El Segundo, California, and initiate partnerships with key defense stakeholders.

